In article <1992Aug18.172536.13138@galileo.cc.rochester.edu>, esot@troi.cc.rochester.edu (Eric Sotnak) writes...
>  I have a blessed magic marker (58) and 6 blank scrolls (ala w. of
>cancellation).  So, I tried writing a scroll of genocide by writing
>"genocide".  The result was a message to the effect that "you don't know how
>to write that."  So what do I need to do?  I also have the option of
>blessing the blank scrolls.  Would that help?  What other scrolls might be
>good to create?

You need to have read a scroll of x before you can write a scroll of x,
and even then, that chance is not guaranteed that you will write it ('In your
haste, you tear the scroll apart!')

So what to write is highly dependant on what you have read.  If you are still
on the low levels (1-10), a scroll of teleportation may come in handy (stores),
while scrolls of enchant weapon/armor are great any time.  The choice is 
yours...

